<h1>Orcraft framework overview</h1>

<h2 id="component-model">Component model</h2>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/Diagrams/Orcraft-Framework.png", "Orcraft component model diagram: the structural hierarchy of suite, group, test and case on the left, the procedural hierarchy of case body, flow and step on the right, and the config, component and result pattern every level shares along the bottom", "large") }}

<p>Orcraft models a test system as a hierarchy of <em>components</em>. Each level owns the level below it
  and contributes its own configuration and its own result.</p>

<table>
  <thead>
    <tr>
      <th>Component</th>
      <th>Base class</th>
      <th>Contains</th>
      <th>You implement</th>
    </tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
    <tr>
      <td><a class="text-accent" href="/framework/suites/">Orcraft Test Suite</a></td>
      <td><code>OrcraftTestSuite</code></td>
      <td>Groups</td>
      <td>Nothing - a suite is declared, not coded</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a class="text-accent" href="/framework/groups/">Orcraft Test Group</a></td>
      <td><code>OrcraftTestGroup</code></td>
      <td>Tests</td>
      <td>Nothing - a group is declared, not coded</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a class="text-accent" href="/framework/test/">Orcraft Test</a></td>
      <td><code>OrcraftTest</code></td>
      <td>Cases</td>
      <td><code>_run_case(case)</code></td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><a class="text-accent" href="/framework/matrix/">Orcraft Test Case</a></td>
      <td><code>OrcraftTestCase</code></td>
      <td>Case cycles</td>
